Commentary of al-Shinqiti (Adwa' al-Bayan) on surah 50, verse 6:

His saying, exalted is He: ﴿Have they not looked at the sky above them, how We built it and adorned it, and it has no rifts?﴾

The hamza (interrogative particle) in His saying "Afa-lam" (Have they not...) governs an omitted element, and the fa' (the conjunctive "fa") is coordinated with it. As we have mentioned many times, this is the more apparent of the two views, and he (al-Shinqiti's source, Ibn Malik) pointed to it in the *Khulasa* (Ibn Malik's *Al-Khulasa*, the versified grammar known as the *Alfiyya*) with his saying:

(p-423) "And the deletion of the thing followed (matbu') is permitted here."

The estimated sense is: Did they turn away from the signs of Allah, so they did not look at the sky above them, how We built it and adorned it, and it has no rifts? That is, there are in it no cracks, no splitting, and no breaking apart. What this noble verse contains of the magnification of the manner in which Allah, exalted is He, built the sky, adorned it, and made it free of splitting and cracks, has all come explained in other verses,

such as His saying, exalted is He, concerning its building: ﴿Are you more difficult to create, or is the sky? He raised its height and made it proportioned﴾ [al-Nazi'at: 27–28];

and His saying: ﴿And the sky We built with might, and indeed We are expanding it﴾ [al-Dhariyat: 47];

and His saying: ﴿And We built above you seven strong ones﴾ [al-Naba': 12];

and His saying: ﴿He who created seven heavens in layers. You see no discrepancy in the creation of the Most Merciful﴾ [al-Mulk: 3];

and His saying: ﴿And We created above you seven paths, and We were not unaware of creation﴾ [al-Mu'minun: 17];

and His saying at the beginning of al-Ra'd: ﴿Allah is He who raised the heavens without pillars that you can see, then He established Himself over the Throne﴾ [al-Ra'd: 2];

and His saying concerning Luqman: ﴿He created the heavens without pillars that you see﴾, the verse [Luqman: 10];

and so on, among other verses.

And

such as His saying, exalted is He, concerning His adornment of the sky: ﴿And We have certainly adorned the nearest sky with lamps, and made them missiles against the devils﴾ [al-Mulk: 5];

and His saying: ﴿And We adorned the nearest sky with lamps and as protection﴾, the verse [Fussilat: 12];

and His saying: ﴿Indeed, We have adorned the nearest sky with the adornment of the stars﴾ [al-Saffat: 6];

and His saying: ﴿And We have certainly placed in the sky constellations and adorned it for the observers﴾ [al-Hijr: 16];

and such as His saying, exalted is He, concerning His preserving the sky from having in it furuj, that is, cracks: ﴿Then return the gaze; do you see any futur?﴾ [al-Mulk: 3]. Al-futur and al-furuj have one meaning, which is cracks and fissures. And His saying, exalted is He: ﴿And We made the sky a protected roof, yet they turn away from its signs﴾ [al-Anbiya': 32].

As for the Day of Resurrection, the sky will split and break apart, and there will be rifts in it, as He, exalted is He, said: ﴿And the day the sky is split open with clouds﴾ [al-Furqan: 25]; and He, exalted is He, said: ﴿So when the sky is split open and becomes red like oil﴾ [al-Rahman: 37]; and He, exalted is He, said: ﴿So on that Day the Inevitable will occur, and the sky will be split apart﴾, the verse [al-Haqqah: 16]; and He, exalted is He, said: ﴿When the sky splits open﴾ ﴿and listens to its Lord and is obligated﴾ [al-Inshiqaq: 1–2]; and He, exalted is He, said: ﴿When the sky breaks apart﴾ [al-Infitar: 1]; and He, exalted is He, said: ﴿A Day that will make children grey-haired﴾ ﴿the sky will be split by it﴾ [al-Muzzammil: 17–18]; and He, exalted is He, said: ﴿So when the stars are obliterated﴾ ﴿and when the sky is opened﴾ [al-Mursalat: 8–9].
